
/datum/patron/divine/astrata
	desc = "The Tyrant of the Gods, sister and counterpart to Noc. Greatest of the Living Gods. She, the <b>RADIANCE</b>, burns away the evils at bay during the dae; and has defined the rights of society for nearly two millenia."

/datum/patron/divine/noc
	desc = "The Reflective Will - and sibling-counterpart to Astrata, aside. In contrast to Solar Will, whose law and diction is absolute, Noc is best described as somewhere between a mirror and a conduit- offering wisdom, insight, wonder and thaumic empowerment to all who look upon them. They share freely what could be learned - and the only judgement cast is the onlooker's own."

/datum/patron/divine/ravox
	desc = "The First Knight, The Blind Bull, Lord of Judgement, Prince of Honor, Ravox is God of Justice. Where Astrata is Divine Order incarnate, Ravox is her General, keeper of the careful balance of what is Righteous and Good and what is Dishonorable and should be Ended.</br> \
	</br> Though what is just does not always fall in line with what is ordered, it is the duty of the Knight to obey His Queen.</br> \
	</br> It is also the duty of the Knight to mind his Lady’s coffers; for blind as He may be, there can be none more careful a banker than He."

/datum/patron/divine/eora
	desc = "Lady of Hearth and Home, Fire-Starter, She Who Ignites The Heart, Matchmaker, Eora is Goddess of Love.</br> \
	</br> No one is quite certain when She first arose, but Her place among the Pentacle is secure- there is no Divine untouched by Love, no mortal safe from Her call. It is She that first made the match that ended so poorly between Moon and Sea, after all, and even now the Tide follows Their glow.</br> \
	</br> Love does not last forever, but however brief, it Changes. </br> \
	</br> Even Death must Dance when Love calls Her to the ballroom."
	worshippers = "Matriarchs, Mothers, Young Unmarried Folk, Poets, Lovers"

/datum/patron/divine/necra
	desc = "Gravemaiden, Lady Inevitable, She Who Comes For Us All, Soultaker and Bonetender, Necra is Goddess of Death. It is Her icy grasp that beckons all mortalkind to the Realms Beyond, and rides upon a pale unicorne - glimpses of which herald an oncoming, and often tragic, end. </br> \
	</br>Even Death can be bargained with, however, and the Gravemaiden is nothing if not patient. It is said that She and Eora are locked often in the throes of dance, as Life and Death must always be, and that the drumming of their matched hearts is unlike any sound known to mortals."

/datum/patron/divine/dendor
	desc = "Lord of Madness, Chaos-Bringer, Prince of Indulgence, He of Feral Heart, Dendor is Nature, and He makes himself known well by the breaking of mortal-wrought confines. </br> \
	</br> Many a highstrung noble has been lured from their hunting saiga and lost deep within His woods, never to be found again, but laughing all the while."

/datum/patron/divine/abyssor
	desc = "The seaborne's Primal Divine. Great Dreamer, He Who Slumbers In The Deep, Saltborne and Wavecrasher, Abyssor is the Sea- violent, and yet calmed. </br> \
	</br> Out of Love long lost, the Tide follows the Moon, and the Moon in turn keeps the Dreamer sleeping within the depths, though the world oft quakes with His fitful slumber.</br> \
	</br> Tyrannical, abyssal, and ne'er to be understood - though those that follow the Deepest Will can court the currents in their favor."

/datum/patron/divine/malum
	desc = "Divine Forgemaster, Master of Invention, Smith of the Gods, it is said that Malum is the Spirit of Humen Creation, patron of all those who make anew what the world has given. Its songs are sung in the pounding of hammer upon steel, the hum and hiss of freshly-quenched blades.</br> \
	</br>To toil is divinity."

/datum/patron/divine/pestra
	desc = "Wormborne Maiden, Lady of Pestilence, Lady of Healing, Bringer of Rot and Regrowth, Patron of Sickness and Recovery, Pestra is one of the oldest Spirits known to humenity. \
	Her life and death occurred in the very first daes of humenkind, and it is through the worship of her that medicine has progressed and lives have become longer and fuller. Praying to the Lady of Rot and Regrowth is said to aide the sickly and soothe the dying."

/datum/patron/divine/xylix

/datum/patron/divine/undivided
	desc = "Five Eternal, Divine Pantheon United, Bulwark against the Darkness. The Five True Divines dilligently watch over their flock granting them potent boons, but not every man catches the attention of merely one. Take lessons from them all, for they are your masters and mentors."
	worshippers = "Commonfolk, Zybantines, Raneshani, the Clergy, and Nobility"
	confess_lines = list(
		"THE HOLY PENTACLE SHALL SHIELD MY SOUL!",
		"I SERVE THE PANTHEON RESPLENDENT!",
		"THE FIVE ETERNAL, FOREVERMORE!",
	)
	titles = list(
		"Gods"
	)
